# Internal planning and process files. These live in the private working repo
# and are deliberately kept out of this one: they are project-management
# scaffolding, not part of the app, and they go stale the moment anyone reads
# them here. Design docs and the decision log ARE published, under docs/.
CLAUDE.md
STATE.md
STATE-archive-*.md
BACKLOG.md
BACKLOG-archive-*.md
DECISIONS-archive-*.md
PONYTAIL-DEBT.md
CLEANUP-REVIEW.md
NEEDS-LAX.md
# Session-to-session handoff notes. Same reasoning as the rest of this block, plus a
# sharper one: a handoff names what is half-done, what is still red and what only the
# owner can do, which is exactly the shape of thing that should not be published.
HANDOFF.md
briefs/
.claude/
docs/plans/
docs/reports/

# Local design/agent tooling, created by the design skill in this working tree.
# Not part of the app, and it carries vendor names and absolute local paths that the
# publishing scan is right to reject. That scan enumerates with `git ls-files`, so these
# are invisible to it until someone stages them - which is exactly what the documented
# `git add -A` pre-commit step does. Ignored so that step stays safe.
.impeccable/
.github/agents/
.github/hooks/
.github/skills/
PRODUCT.md

# Local knowledge-graph output from the graphify skill. Regeneratable, and it
# extracts content from files already gitignored above (HANDOFF.md, CLAUDE.md).
graphify-out/
